  "description": "Single-storey side extension at 72 & 74 Bransgrove road and conversion of 2 single dwelling houses into 4 x\nflats comprising 2 x 2-bed 3-person flats, 1 x 1-bed 2-person at and 1\nstudio flat, with associated parking, amenity, refuse and cycle storage.\n",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:0cm; text-align:justify; padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of the loss of existing semi detached housing and the failure to provide any family sized homes with three or more bedrooms, the proposed development would fail to achieve an appropriate housing mix and would not contribute to local housing need or the creation of inclusive and mixed communities, contrary to the provisions of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policy H10 of the London Plan 2021, Policy CS1 I of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), policy DM24 and of the Harrow Development Management Policies (2013) and Draft policies HO1 (A 1.i) and HO2(1b) of the Emerging Harrow&amp;nbsp;New Local Plan&amp;nbsp;(2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br data-cke-eol=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
